From: postmaster@${DOMAIN}
To: ${USER_EMAIL}
Subject: Welcome! Corporate Email and Global Address List (GAL) Setup Guide
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
  .card { border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; max-width: 680px; margin: 20px auto; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); }
  .header { border-bottom: 2px solid #3182ce; padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .header h2 { color: #2b6cb0; margin: 0; }
  .step-box { background: #f7fafc; border-left: 4px solid #3182ce; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }
  code { background: #edf2f7; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, monospace; color: #c53030; }
  pre { background: #1a202c; color: #e2e8f0; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .footer { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #718096; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 12px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="card">
  <div class="header">
    <h2>🎉 Welcome aboard! Corporate Email & Address Book Guide</h2>
  </div>
  <p>Dear <strong>${USER_NAME}</strong>,</p>
  <p>Your enterprise email account <code>${USER_EMAIL}</code> has been activated! Please follow the instructions below to configure Outlook or your mobile devices to enable smart search in the internal Global Address List (GAL).</p>

  <div class="step-box">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:#2d3748;">📌 Server Connection Details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Incoming Mail (IMAP):</strong> <code>${MAIL_SERVER}</code> (Port <code>993</code> / SSL)</li>
      <li><strong>Outgoing Mail (SMTP):</strong> <code>${MAIL_SERVER}</code> (Port <code>465</code> or <code>587</code> / SSL)</li>
      <li><strong>Address Book Directory (LDAP/LDAPS):</strong> <code>${MAIL_SERVER}</code> (Port <code>3268</code> Plain / No Cert, or <code>3269</code> SSL)</li>
      <li><strong>Username:</strong> <code>${USER_NAME}</code> (Account name only, without @${DOMAIN})</li>
      <li><strong>Password:</strong> Your Windows AD domain password</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="step-box">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:#2d3748;">📖 Outlook Address Book Configuration Steps</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Outlook ➔ Click <strong>"File"</strong> ➔ <strong>"Account Settings"</strong> ➔ <strong>"Address Books"</strong> tab.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"New..."</strong> ➔ Select <strong>"Internet Directory Service (LDAP)"</strong>.</li>
      <li>Server Name: enter <code>${MAIL_SERVER}</code>.</li>
      <li>Check <strong>"This server requires me to log on"</strong>, enter User Name: <code>${USER_NAME}</code> and your domain password.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"More Settings ..."</strong>:
        <ul>
          <li>Under the "Connection" tab, set Port to <strong><code>3268</code></strong> (<strong>Uncheck</strong> SSL), or set to <strong><code>3269</code></strong> with "Use Secure Sockets Layer (SSL)" checked.</li>
          <li>Under the "Search" tab, select <strong>"Custom"</strong> search base and enter <code>${SEARCH_BASE}</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Click OK and restart Outlook. When composing emails, typing colleague names will auto-complete contacts!</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    <p>This automated message was sent upon account provisioning. For technical support, please contact the IT Service Desk.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
